<title>ARGENTINA: Union chief says Escondida strike likely to go on.</title>
<headline>Union chief says Escondida strike likely to go on.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unionized workers at Chile's Escondida copper mine are likely to vote Wednesday to continue striking, their union president said.</p>
<p>&quot;The feeling at the moment is that the strike is going to continue,&quot; union president Hugo Fernandez told Reuters by telephone from the northern Chilean city of Antofagasta, &quot;The workers' wives are very upset and want the strike to continue.&quot;</p>
</text>
